<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  task: Complete a two-color rectangular crop into the full 20x20 binary motif
  motif:
    shape: 20x20 fixed binary pattern (hard-coded in solver as _BASE_PATTERN)
    fg_density: 42.2% (169/400 cells)
    dihedral_variants: 8 distinct orientations (rot0/90/180/270 x flip), none identical or complementary
  input:
    grid: rectangular sub-window of one dihedral variant, painted with 2 colors
    rows: 8-16
    cols: 8-12
    area: 80-156 cells
    colors: exactly 2 distinct ARC colors; any pair [observed]
    uniqueness: crop must uniquely identify (variant, offset, fg/bg polarity) -- solver asserts exactly 1 match
    uniqueness_guarantee: 100% for min(H,W)>=11 or max(H,W)>=12; ~95-99% for smaller crops
  output:
    grid: always 20x20
    content: full motif in matched orientation, fg->color_a, bg->color_b

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick 2 distinct ARC colors (fg, bg).
    2. Pick a random dihedral variant index (0-7) to get the 20x20 boolean pattern.
    3. Build the full 20x20 output grid -- fg where pattern is True, bg where False.
    4. Choose crop dimensions H in [8,16], W in [8,12].
    5. Choose random offset (r, c) with r in [0, 20-H], c in [0, 20-W].
    6. Extract the HxW sub-window from the output as the input.
    7. Verify uniqueness -- the crop must match exactly 1 (variant, offset, polarity) across all 8 variants x 2 polarities. Reject and re-pick offset if not unique.
  notes: |
    For min(H,W)>=11 or max(H,W)>=12, uniqueness is guaranteed (0% rejection).
    For smaller crops, rejection rate is <=5% so retry is fine.
```
